From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:36:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: a log line reaches the pipe before the next one, even
 across a crash

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The log goes to stderr, which the shell reads through a pipe; a line stayed in the stream's buffer until the next
 one pushed it out, so a crash kept the last lines - the only ones that say what the game was doing - from ever
 reaching the log. Each line is flushed now.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/host/hle_bigstack.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_bigstack.c b/dm/host/hle_bigstack.c
index 7c7ec77..f2ae97b 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_bigstack.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_bigstack.c
@@ -174,7 +174,9 @@ void *dm_bigstack_caller(void *ra) {
 // dm_bigstack_enter as a take-over is, with the argument list by address, so on a guest stack it runs on the host stack and anywhere else it is jumped to directly
 static void log_emit(const char *fmt, va_list *ap) __attribute__((used));
 static void log_emit(const char *fmt, va_list *ap) {
-    flockfile(stderr); vfprintf(stderr, fmt, *ap); fputc('\n', stderr); funlockfile(stderr);
+    // fflush matters more than it looks: the log is a pipe to the shell, a crash takes whatever is still buffered
+    // with it, and the last lines before a crash are the only ones that say what the game was doing.
+    flockfile(stderr); vfprintf(stderr, fmt, *ap); fputc('\n', stderr); fflush(stderr); funlockfile(stderr);
 }
 void log_emit_bs(const char *fmt, va_list *ap);
 __asm__(".text\n.p2align 2\n.globl _log_emit_bs\n.private_extern _log_emit_bs\n_log_emit_bs:\n"
